      "body": "## Overview\n\nFix Unlimited-OCR's underestimated maximum image-token bound, which can reject valid images with a small encoder budget.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Use a 1×32 profiling crop grid to cover the maximum number of newline features.\n- Correct the default per-image bound from 3553 to 3793 tokens.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_unlimited_ocr.py -v\n```\n\n- New regression: 1 passed; it fails on the original code. Existing processor regression tests: 9 passed. Pre-commit passed.\n- Actual `baidu/Unlimited-OCR` serving, BF16 / TP=1, official nightly `0.32.0rc1.dev190+g3f1bcfd82`, using a 640×20480 image:\n\n| `max_num_batched_tokens` | Original | Patched |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2048 | HTTP 400: 3793 image tokens exceed the 3553 cache | HTTP 200 |\n| 8192 | HTTP 200 | HTTP 200 |\n\nSmall, ordinary, tall and wide synthetic inputs were compared. Same-budget default compile/graph comparisons preserve output tokens and sampled-token logprobs exactly.\n\nServing used `TRITON_ALLOW_NON_CONSTEXPR_GLOBALS=1` for an unrelated nightly compile issue. Baseline OCR on some synthetic inputs is empty or incorrect; validation covers request acceptance and output regression, without an accuracy claim.\n\n## Details\n\nBoth 4×8 and 1×32 grids contain 32 crops, but the latter has more feature rows and therefore more newline tokens. It reaches the true upper bound without changing inference computation.\n\nNo matching open fix was found. Related [#54527](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54527) concerns processor kwargs rather than this default crop-grid bound.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n\n</details>\n\n",
